&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;134233117&amp;quot;:false,&amp;quot;134233118&amp;quot;:false,&amp;quot;335551550&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335551620&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559738&amp;quot;:240,&amp;quot;335559739&amp;quot;:240}&quot;&gt;By submitting your application, you consent to Anduril Industries using a third-party service provider to conduct pre-employment risk, integrity, and due diligence screening and assessing potential risks as part of your application process. This third-party service provider provides risk-intelligence services that may include analysis of sanctions and watchlists, adverse media, public-record information, and other lawful open-source or commercial data sources. This third-party service provider does not act as a consumer reporting agency. Use of this provider helps to ensure compliance with applicable laws and protect technology, intellectual property, and organizational security.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

a16z-anduril-industries:greenhouse:50293.descriptionHtml:
&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Anduril Industries is a defense technology company with a mission to transform U.S. and allied military capabilities with advanced technology. By bringing the expertise, technology, and business model of the 21st century’s most innovative companies to the defense industry, Anduril is changing how military systems are designed, built and sold. Anduril’s family of systems is powered by Lattice OS, an AI-powered operating system that turns thousands of data streams into a realtime, 3D command and control center. As the world enters an era of strategic competition, Anduril is committed to bringing cutting-edge autonomy, AI, computer vision, sensor fusion, and networking technology to the military in months, not years.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3&gt;ABOUT THE TEAM&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Anduril&#39;s Electronic Warfare (EW) division builds next-generation electronic warfare platforms that integrate with the broader Anduril Lattice ecosystem. The Mission Engineering team is responsible for ensuring these systems are operationally ready, successfully deployed, and continuously supported for customers in the field. We own the bridge between engineering development and real-world mission success.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;ABOUT THE JOB&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a Lead Mission Software Engineer to build and lead the EW mission engineering function. In this role, you will own the operational readiness and field success of our electronic warfare products. You will lead a team of mission software engineers responsible for production support, system deployment, field issue resolution, and rapid software fixes to meet urgent customer needs. You will act as the technical owner for mission system delivery from installation through sustainment, collaborating closely with embedded software, applications engineering, and test/QA teams to ensure our products perform reliably in operational environments.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Above all, this role demands a &quot;Whatever It Takes&quot; mindset, executing in an expedient, scalable, and pragmatic way while keeping the mission top-of-mind and making sound engineering decisions to deliver successful outcomes correctly, on-time, and with high quality.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;WHAT YOU&#39;LL DO&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead and grow a team of mission engineers supporting EW product deployments and field operations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own customer success through the delivery, installation, and sustainment of operational EW systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Triage field issues, drive root cause analysis, and coordinate rapid fixes across software and hardware teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide technical leadership and hands-on contributions across deployed system troubleshooting, software patching, and system configuration&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish processes for incident response, post-incident review, and preventive measures&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with embedded software engineering and applications engineering to ensure mission-critical fixes are incorporated into future releases&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with end-users to understand operational needs, translate them into engineering action, and balance urgency with engineering quality&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Engage with customers to represent technical aspects of system performance and operational readiness&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate with test/QA and release engineering to qualify builds for field deployment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Travel up to 30% to support deployments, integration events, demonstrations, and customer engagements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;REQUIRED QUALIFICATIONS&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;7+ years professional experience in software engineering, systems engineering, or technical operations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2+ years in a technical leadership role (leading teams, setting objectives, driving execution)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Haskell or Rust, as well as TypeScript codebases&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience troubleshooting and supporting remotely deployed software/hardware systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience with Linux system administration and debugging in production environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work across the software stack — from embedded systems through networking and application layers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience engaging with customers to represent technical capabilities and coordinate on operational needs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong communication skills and ability to collaborate across engineering, program management, and operations teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to operate in unstructured environments and drive issues to resolution&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Eligible to obtain and maintain an active U.S. Top Secret SCI security clearance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Willingness to take on-call responsibilities as needed to support production systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Willingness to travel up to 30%&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with electronic warfare systems, software-defined radio, or RF systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with containerized deployments (Kubernetes, Docker) in operational environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with distributed communication networks and system-of-systems architectures&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with CI/CD pipelines and release management processes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Nix/NixOS&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior experience in defense technology or military operations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to mentor engineers, build team cohesion, and increase team capability&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;US Salary Range&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$191,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$253,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;The salary range for this role is an estimate based on a wide range of compensation factors, inclusive of base salary only. Actual salary offer may vary based on (but not limited to) work experience, education and/or training, critical skills, and/or business considerations. Highly competitive equity grants are included in the majority of full time offers; and are considered part of Anduril&#39;s total compensation package. Additionally, Anduril offers top-tier benefits for full-time employees, including:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;134233117&amp;quot;:false,&amp;quot;134233118&amp;quot;:false,&amp;quot;335551550&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335551620&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559738&amp;quot;:240,&amp;quot;335559739&amp;quot;:240}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
